// soup-server.h, soup-server-message.h: SoupServer, an HTTP/1.1 server on
// the GLib main context, as libsoup's: it listens on sockets of its own (or
// ones given), reads each connection's requests one after another without
// blocking, gives them to the handler of the longest path that covers
// them (early handlers once the headers are in, auth domains before them,
// WebSocket handlers for upgrades), and writes the responses (Content-
// Length, chunked or to the end of the connection; a handler may pause a
// message and add to a chunked body as it goes). Connections are kept
// while both sides allow. TLS servers are not here (mlx-glib's TLS backend
// is a client's): listening with SOUP_SERVER_LISTEN_HTTPS fails.
//
// A SoupServerMessage's private data is a pointer to a record:
//   0 the connection           8 the auth domain        16 the auth user
//  24 the remote address's text 32 the method (interned)
//  40 the HTTP version, 44 the version the request had
//  48 the status, 56 the reason phrase, 64 the URI
//  72 the request body, 80 its headers, 88 the response body, 96 its headers
// 104 whether the connection's I/O is this message's
// 108 whether it is "OPTIONS *", 112 the TLS peer certificate, 120 its errors
//
// A connection (no GObject: libsoup's SoupServerConnection is private) is
// a record:
//   0 the server             8 the GIOStream          16 the GSocket
//  24 the input stream      32 the output stream
//  40 the local address     48 the remote address (GSocketAddresses)
//  56 the message being read or answered
//  64 what was read and not taken (a buffer), 72 where it starts, 80 ends,
//  88 its size
//  96 the I/O's source      104 whether it is connected
// 108 whether the I/O is running
// 112 the read state, 116 the write state (io.mlx's states)
// 120 the request body's encoding, 124 the response's
// 128 the request body left (Content-Length), 136 the response body left
// 144 the bytes to write, 152 how many, 160 how many went
// 168 where in the response body writing is, 176 the chunk being written
// 184 whether the message is paused, 188 whether the server read it
// 192 the unpause source
// 200 the request chunk left, 208 the chunked coding's phase
// 212 whether the input ended, 216 the references
const m = @import("../glib/memory.mlx")
const g = @import("./g.mlx")
const c = @import("./common.mlx")
